# =====================================================================
# Saleor Attributes domain — P2 wave, packet A2b: the attribute read
# roots (the canonical plan §5-P2: "product types and typed attributes,
# products, variants/options ... map to existing catalog/search/media
# owners" — the declared continuation of the campaign-b2-a2 product-type
# slice, which marked attribute/attributes NOT_STARTED).
# PROPOSAL to A0 (the one SDL steward): the Query fields below append to
# the shared root type Query; every other declaration in this fragment
# is a PURE ADDITION — no existing shared type is redeclared (PageInfo,
# OrderDirection, PermissionEnum, the User/Group families, the
# ProductType* family and the StoreProduct* family keep their existing
# declarations — including the legacy StoreProductTypeAttribute/
# StoreProductAttributeOption/StoreProductAttributeValue types with
# their own attribute vocabulary).
# Root names, argument names/types/nullability and the connection
# envelope are the pinned Saleor 3.23.43 wire contract
# (saleor/graphql/schema.graphql, blob b8fa0dd8 — the measured roots
# attribute/attributes at schema lines 1421/1455, the Attribute type at
# line 3684, AttributeCountableConnection/Edge at lines 10770/10779,
# AttributeFilterInput at line 10787, AttributeWhereInput at line
# 10819, AttributeSortingInput/AttributeSortField at lines 17932/17940);
# the platform's catalog owner remains the single source of truth behind
# them. The GLOBAL IDs on this surface are the typed Relay-style codec's
# (SaleorGlobalIdCodec): opaque base64("Attribute:<uuid>") values —
# never raw UUIDs.
#
# The bounded Attribute projection (the honest method the User/Group/
# ProductType read slices established): the platform's
# catalog_attribute_definitions row (V237) owns id/code/nameEn/nameAr/
# value_type/description. DECLARED fields are owned facts only:
#   - id: the typed global ID over the native UUID primary key;
#   - name: the rendered primary display name (nameEn when present, else
#     nameAr — the bilingual row's own at-least-one guarantee makes it
#     non-null; the AR dimension stays with the owning bilingual model
#     until a translation owner exists — the registered translation
#     divergence row);
#   - slug: the row's immutable public code (the entity's own lowercase
#     slug validation IS the Saleor slug contract);
#   - inputType: the closed domain value shape's Saleor rendering —
#     TEXT→PLAIN_TEXT, NUMBER→NUMERIC, BOOLEAN→BOOLEAN, CHOICE→DROPDOWN
#     (the platform's free text is plain text, never rich text; its
#     CHOICE holds exactly one registered option, never a multiselect);
#   - withChoices: the CHOICE-typed fact (value_type = 'CHOICE').
# UNDECLARED Attribute fields, each with its reason (a declared-but-fake
# field would be the violation, not the absence):
#   - privateMetadata/privateMetafield/privateMetadata(s)/metadata/
#     metafield/metafields: no metadata capability on attribute
#     definitions yet.
#   - entityType/referenceTypes: no reference/entity attribute
#     capability — the closed domain vocabulary is TEXT/NUMBER/BOOLEAN/
#     CHOICE (chk_catalog_attr_type).
#   - type (AttributeTypeEnum PRODUCT_TYPE/PAGE_TYPE/CUSTOMER_TYPE): no
#     owning classification column on catalog_attribute_definitions; the
#     assignment rows exist (product_type_attribute_assignments) but a
#     definition may be unassigned, so upstream's non-null classification
#     cannot be derived honestly.
#   - unit: no measurement-unit fact on the platform.
#   - choices: the owning options table EXISTS (catalog_attribute_options,
#     position-ordered, V237) — but the nested
#     AttributeValueCountableConnection surface (its own
#     AttributeValue/AttributeValueCountableConnection/Edge +
#     AttributeChoicesSortingInput/AttributeChoicesSortField +
#     AttributeValueFilterInput/AttributeValueWhereInput closure) lands
#     with its own slice when the Dashboard journey needs it; declared
#     then, not silently faked now.
#   - valueRequired: an ASSIGNMENT-level fact
#     (product_type_attribute_assignments.is_required), not a definition
#     fact — a definition is required on one product type and optional
#     on another, so no single honest non-null value exists.
#   - visibleInStorefront/filterableInStorefront/filterableInDashboard/
#     availableInGrid/storefrontSearchPosition: no owning columns (the
#     last four are deprecated no-effect flags upstream too).
#   - translation: no translation owner (the registered translation
#     divergence keeps the AR dimension with the bilingual model).
#   - productTypes/productVariantTypes: the assignment rows own the
#     facts, but the nested ProductTypeCountableConnection surfaces land
#     with their own slices.
#   - externalReference: no external-reference capability on the
#     platform.
# AttributeInputTypeEnum is declared BOUNDED to the four values the
# closed domain vocabulary renders (DROPDOWN/NUMERIC/PLAIN_TEXT/
# BOOLEAN); MULTISELECT/FILE/REFERENCE/SINGLE_REFERENCE/RICH_TEXT/
# SWATCH/DATE/DATE_TIME stay undeclared — no owning value shape maps to
# them (the same honest method the bounded ProductType closure used).
# The declared-but-unexecuted root arguments (filter, where, search,
# channel, before, last, the unowned sortBy fields, and the attribute
# root's externalReference) answer explicit classified
# IllegalArgumentExceptions at runtime — the staffUsers precedent —
# never a silent no-op, never fake success. The sort vocabulary is
# Saleor's own AttributeSortField enum (all nine values verbatim,
# upstream's deprecation notes included): NAME and SLUG execute as real
# forward-only keyset sorts (rendered name / immutable code, each with
# the id tiebreaker); VALUE_REQUIRED, IS_VARIANT_ONLY,
# VISIBLE_IN_STOREFRONT and the four deprecated flags have no owning
# column and answer the explicit classified not-implemented error. The
# attribute root's executable keys are id (the typed global ID) and
# slug (the owner's code lookup, upstream's id-first precedence); a
# keyless call answers the classified validation error — the recorded
# divergence from upstream's null answer. Both roots require Saleor
# staff permissions (MANAGE_PRODUCTS-class) — enforced server-side as
# the platform's ADMIN capability at the catalog use-case boundary (the
# RBAC mapping registry row), never as a UI route guard.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Query additions (append to the shared root type Query)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
type Query {
    # "List of the shop's attributes." — the typed attribute reference
    # collection with its countable-connection envelope (edges/pageInfo/
    # totalCount, byte-shape from the pinned schema). FORWARD-ONLY
    # keyset paging on this first slice: first/after ride the platform's
    # ScrollPosition keyset contract (the staffUsers/permissionGroups/
    # productTypes precedent — cursors identify a row's sort key (the
    # executed sort field, id), never an absolute offset); before/last
    # stay declared (the exact Saleor argument shape) but answer an
    # explicit classified error until a backward scroll exists — a
    # recorded, tested boundary, not a silent no-op. filter (deprecated
    # upstream), where, search and channel are likewise the declared
    # wire shapes with explicit not-yet-supported errors. The sort
    # vocabulary is Saleor's own AttributeSortField enum: NAME and SLUG
    # execute as real keyset sorts, deterministic with the id
    # tiebreaker; the other seven values answer the explicit
    # not-implemented error.
    attributes(
    """Filtering options for attributes."""
    filter: AttributeFilterInput @deprecated(reason: "Use `where` filter instead.")

    """Where filtering options for attributes."""
    where: AttributeWhereInput

    """Search attributes."""
    search: String

    """Sorting options for attributes."""
    sortBy: AttributeSortingInput

    """Slug of a channel for which the data should be returned."""
    channel: String

    """Return the elements in the list that come before the specified cursor."""
    before: String

    """Return the elements in the list that come after the specified cursor."""
    after: String

    """Retrieve the first n elements from the list."""
    first: Int

    """Retrieve the last n elements from the list."""
    last: Int
    ): AttributeCountableConnection

    # "Look up an attribute by ID, slug or external reference." — the
    # staff lookup over the typed global ID (Saleor requires staff
    # permissions → ADMIN here, enforced in the owning catalog use
    # case). id executes through the typed global-ID codec; slug
    # executes through the owner's code lookup (upstream's id-first
    # precedence when both are sent). An unknown but well-formed key
    # answers null (the safe absence); a malformed or mistyped global ID
    # answers the codec's classified validation error — never a raw UUID
    # fallback. externalReference has no owning capability and answers
    # the explicit classified error whenever it is sent; a keyless call
    # answers the classified validation error (the recorded divergence
    # from upstream's null answer).
    attribute(
    """ID of the attribute."""
    id: ID

    """Slug of the attribute."""
    slug: String

    """External ID of the attribute."""
    externalReference: String
    ): Attribute
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bounded Attribute projection — see the block comment above for
# the closure policy. id is the typed global ID over the native
# catalog_attribute_definitions key; name is the bilingual row's
# rendered primary display name; slug is the row's immutable public
# code; inputType is the closed domain value shape's Saleor rendering;
# withChoices is the CHOICE-typed fact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
type Attribute {
    """The ID of the attribute — typed global ID (opaque, never a raw UUID)."""
    id: ID!

    """Name of the attribute (the rendered primary display name)."""
    name: String!

    """Slug of the attribute (the row's immutable public code)."""
    slug: String!

    """The input type to use for entering attribute values in the dashboard (the closed domain value shape's rendering)."""
    inputType: AttributeInputTypeEnum

    """Flag indicating that attribute has predefined choices (the definition is CHOICE-typed)."""
    withChoices: Boolean!
}

# Saleor's connection envelope for countable attribute lists —
# declared (not runtime-generated) so the exact Saleor shape stands,
# including totalCount. Spring's ConnectionTypeDefinitionConfigurer skips
# already-declared connection types (the measured declared-types-skip
# behavior the UserCountableConnection/GroupCountableConnection/
# ProductTypeCountableConnection declarations recorded), so this
# declaration wins and the generated connections elsewhere are
# untouched. pageInfo reuses the EXISTING shared PageInfo type — not
# redeclared.
type AttributeCountableConnection {
    """Pagination data for this connection."""
    pageInfo: PageInfo!

    edges: [AttributeCountableEdge!]!

    """A total count of items in the collection."""
    totalCount: Int
}

type AttributeCountableEdge {
    """The item at the end of the edge."""
    node: Attribute!

    """A cursor for use in pagination (the row's keyset sort key)."""
    cursor: String!
}

# The bounded input-type vocabulary — only the four values the closed
# domain value shape (TEXT/NUMBER/BOOLEAN/CHOICE, V237's
# chk_catalog_attr_type) renders; the other eight upstream values stay
# undeclared until an owning value shape exists (see the block comment
# above).
enum AttributeInputTypeEnum {
    """Predefined choices selected from a dropdown (the CHOICE value shape)."""
    DROPDOWN

    """A numeric value (the NUMBER value shape)."""
    NUMERIC

    """A plain text value (the TEXT value shape — plain, never rich text)."""
    PLAIN_TEXT

    """A boolean value (the BOOLEAN value shape)."""
    BOOLEAN
}

# Saleor's attribute filter input — the declared wire shape of the
# deprecated filter argument (see attributes: an explicit classified
# error until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure:
# search/ids/slugs carry the scalar filter surface; valueRequired (an
# assignment-level fact), isVariantOnly and visibleInStorefront (no
# owning columns), metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter closure), type
# (the unowned PRODUCT_TYPE/PAGE_TYPE/CUSTOMER_TYPE classification),
# inCollection/inCategory (no collection/category relation on
# definitions) and the deprecated no-effect flags stay undeclared until
# an owning capability exists — any filter use answers the classified
# not-implemented error before field-level semantics matter, and a
# Dashboard query naming an undeclared sub-field fails schema
# validation loudly (never a silent no-op).
input AttributeFilterInput {
    search: String
    ids: [ID!]
    slugs: [String!]
}

# Saleor's attribute where input — the declared wire shape of the where
# argument (see attributes: an explicit classified error until the
# owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids and withChoices
# carry the owned scalar facts; metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
# closure), name/slug (the generic StringFilterInput input is not yet
# declared by any integrated slice), inputType/entityType/type/unit
# (enum filter inputs over unowned facts), inCollection/inCategory,
# valueRequired (assignment-level fact), visibleInStorefront, the
# deprecated filterableInDashboard flag and the AND/OR composition
# capability stay undeclared until an owning capability exists — any
# where use answers the classified not-implemented error.
input AttributeWhereInput {
    ids: [ID!]
    withChoices: Boolean
}

# Saleor's attribute sorting input and field vocabulary — the full
# pinned enum is declared verbatim (nine values with upstream's own
# deprecation notes); NAME and SLUG execute as real keyset sorts, the
# other seven answer the explicit not-implemented error. direction
# reuses the EXISTING shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
input AttributeSortingInput {
    """Specifies the direction in which to sort attributes."""
    direction: OrderDirection!

    """Sort attributes by the selected field."""
    field: AttributeSortField!
}

enum AttributeSortField {
    """Sort attributes by name"""
    NAME

    """Sort attributes by slug"""
    SLUG

    """Sort attributes by the value required flag"""
    VALUE_REQUIRED

    """Sort attributes by the variant only flag"""
    IS_VARIANT_ONLY

    """Sort attributes by visibility in the storefront"""
    VISIBLE_IN_STOREFRONT

    """Sort attributes by the filterable in storefront flag"""
    FILTERABLE_IN_STOREFRONT @deprecated(reason: "This flag is not used by Saleor. Keep the logic in the storefront or use `Attribute` metadata instead.")

    """Sort attributes by the filterable in dashboard flag"""
    FILTERABLE_IN_DASHBOARD @deprecated(reason: "This flag is not used by Saleor. Keep the logic in the dashboard or use `Attribute` metadata instead.")

    """Sort attributes by their position in storefront"""
    STOREFRONT_SEARCH_POSITION @deprecated(reason: "This flag is not used by Saleor. Keep the logic in the storefront or use `Attribute` metadata instead.")

    """Sort attributes based on whether they can be displayed or not in a product grid."""
    AVAILABLE_IN_GRID @deprecated(reason: "This flag is not used by Saleor. Keep the logic in the storefront or use `Attribute` metadata instead.")
}
